<title>UK: CRICKET-RAIN WASHES OUT FIRST DAY OF SECOND TEST.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-RAIN WASHES OUT FIRST DAY OF SECOND TEST.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rain washed out the opening day of the second test between England and Australia on Thursday without a ball being bowled.</p>
<p>Rain fell throughout the afternoon,  forcing the umpires to call off play for the day just before five p.m. (1600 GMT) .</p>
</text>
